# Project 2 — Support Ticket Automation

## Project overview

Project 2 is a practical Microsoft Power Automate support-ticket system built through multiple incremental exercises.

The project demonstrates how support requests can be created manually, processed on a schedule and generated automatically from incoming emails.

## Project components

### 1. Recurring and instant flows

This module demonstrates:

- scheduled cloud flows
- manually triggered flows
- trigger inputs
- Excel ticket creation
- email notifications
- run history
- basic troubleshooting

[Open recurring and instant flows](recurring_and_instant_flow/README.md)

### 2. Email ticket intake

This module demonstrates:

- Outlook email triggers
- attachment downloading
- OneDrive file creation
- subject-line parsing
- Apply to each loops
- automatic Excel ticket creation

[Open email ticket intake](email_ticket_intake/README.md)

## Current flow architecture

```text
Scheduled flow
→ checks the support-ticket table
→ sends a status email

Manual flow
→ accepts ticket information
→ creates an Excel ticket
→ sends a confirmation email

Email intake flow
→ receives an Outlook email
→ parses its subject
→ saves its attachments
→ creates an Excel ticket
```

